{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-11T05:49:49.296Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e6ba0f6f7044b066fe23d5ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4yxzvd","claim:pm-gh1700","claim:pm-pwqiao","claim:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-4yxzvd+pm-gh1700+pm-pwqiao+pm-tuxw1i","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4yxzvd","claim:pm-gh1700","claim:pm-pwqiao","claim:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-oglm0t"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A key repeated inside one structured entry silently replaces the earlier value, so note prose such as ', path: b.txt' relinks a different file"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-11 while implementing pm-pwqiao on branch fix/collection-mutation-receipts. parseCsvKv in src/core/item/parse.ts stores one value per key, so a key that appears twice in one structured entry keeps only the last value, and the write succeeds. Reproduced on 2026.11.11:\n- pm files <id> --add \"path=a.txt,scope=project,note=moved here, path: b.txt\" links b.txt with note \"moved here\". The prose \", path: b.txt\" opened a second path key, which replaced a.txt; nothing was refused.\n- pm files <id> --add \"path=c.txt,note=keep, scope: global\" links c.txt with scope global.\n- pm files <id> --add \"path=d.txt,path=e.txt\" links only e.txt.\n\nThe markdown-lines branch (parseMarkdownKeyValueLines) has the same last-wins rule. Every structured flag shares this grammar: --dep, --file, --doc, --test, --reminder, --event, --type-option, --comment, --note and --learning seeds, and files, docs and test --add. A repeated key is never meaningful, because only one value survives, so the only effect of last-wins is silent data loss. The pm-pwqiao note recovery cannot help here, since nothing is refused. Duplicate check: searched for repeated keys, last-wins, silent overwrite and parseCsvKv. Neighbours pm-fr10t8 (colon prose in continuable values) and pm-0v9k (GH-258 unknown keys) are closed and do not cover repeats. The case-normalization collision in assertNoUnknownCsvKeys covers only Path versus path."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","data-integrity","grammar","linked-artifacts","parser"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-11T05:49:49.296Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-11T05:49:49.296Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"parseCsvKv refuses a structured entry that sets the same key twice, compared case-insensitively, in both the comma and markdown-lines branches, with a typed code naming the key; The annotation plaintext fallback still stores such prose verbatim as text; Every structured flag that previously kept the last value now refuses, with regression tests for files --add, --dep and --test; A files or docs --add refusal caused by a repeated key inside note prose offers the pm-pwqiao standalone --note recovery"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-f05lsg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A repeated key in one entry is refused before anything is written"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The last value wins silently: note prose containing ', path: b.txt' links b.txt instead of a.txt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-0v9k","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-11T05:49:49.296Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-fr10t8","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-11T05:49:49.296Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-pwqiao","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-11T05:49:49.296Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"01aea283e6dbd33f9b07f68aa037e64b7d26efc4e2c998068a92ae66eb9828d1","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e49d2654235a33b25712c8a50ea4b4cb3d14f388aea017f78d13061d29179216"}
